<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the League of Cambrai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1508–<a href="/years/1516">1516</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as War of the Holy League · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the League of Cambrai was fought from 1508 to 1516 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a>. It began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a>, Emperor Maximilian I and Ferdinand of Aragon allied against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, which was routed at Agnadello in 1509; the alliances then shifted repeatedly, and by 1516 Venice had recovered most of its mainland territory.</p></div>
